Package: cohortHarmonize
Title: Config-Driven Harmonization and Quality Control for Longitudinal Cohort Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Luke", "Monnich", email = "lukemonnich03@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A source-agnostic, metadata-driven toolkit for retrospectively
    harmonizing longitudinal cohort datasets onto a shared DataSchema and grading
    the result with a formal data-quality framework (the four dimensions of
    Schmidt et al. 2021: integrity, completeness, consistency, accuracy). Raw data
    can be read from CSV files, a REDCap API, statistical formats (SAS/SPSS/Stata)
    or a database connection. A federated mode lets each site harmonize its own
    data locally so that only harmonized outputs -- never raw records -- are
    combined. Originally developed to harmonize the PEG and HBS Parkinson's cohorts.
